# PAGE 11 — DATA & TRUST CENTRE

## 70. Source registry and coverage

Page header `Data & Trust`, selected farm/field/report context, sections `Coverage`, `Sources`, `Values`, `Methods`, `Data gaps`, `Audit history`. For each data source show actual provider/product, variables, official link, current integration status (`Live`, `Configured but unverified`, `Planned`, `Unavailable`), resolution, temporal cadence/range, latest observation/acquisition and retrieval times, attribution/terms, quality caveats and whether it contributed to this report. Do not badge a planned source as connected because its name appears in code/docs.

Potential categories: NASA POWER meteorological/solar history; NASA SMAP soil moisture at actual product resolution; MODIS valid vegetation/ET/land-cover products; NASADEM terrain if connected; GPM IMERG rainfall cross-check; SoilGrids as non-NASA soil prior; Sentinel-2/NASA HLS only after real imagery processing is integrated; a named forecast provider for short-range weather. These are not automatically all installed.

Per-variable coverage displays value/availability, unit, spatial scale, observed period, retrieved time, source quality and impact on analysis. Current retrieval time is not observation time. If grid resolution exceeds field extent, explain that it is broader context, not exact field-specific sensing.

## 71. Shared evidence drawer

Every important number should open one shared evidence drawer from Home, Map, Farm Detail, Rotation Planner and Farm Intelligence. It contains metric/value/unit; time/window/timezone; farm/field and geometry version; source/product/link; resolution and aggregation; quality flags; observed/modelled/estimated/farmer-entered type; actual formula/inputs/model version; limitations/confidence; related report/alert/recommendation IDs. Use shared component and same provenance model everywhere; don't write contradictory descriptions on different pages.

## 72. Methods, gaps and audit history

Each method entry includes purpose, inputs, units, equation/algorithm, references, assumptions, expected range, validation tests, version, limitations and UI use. Do not call a rough proxy FAO-56. Data Gap Coach ranks missing inputs as critical for current analysis, helpful or context-only and routes directly to add them; do not promise a numerical confidence gain unless validated. Audit history records profile/geometry edits, schedule consent, management input, plan activation and report runs with actor/time/action/object ID while avoiding secret or excessive personal content.

