# PAGE 12 — SETTINGS, PRIVACY, GLOBAL SEARCH, NOTIFICATIONS, AI AGRONOMIST AND GUIDE

## 73. Settings structure

Use sections `Preferences`, `Display`, `Notifications`, `Units & time`, `Privacy & data`, `Automation`, `Connected services`, `Account`, `Export & deletion`. Do not add billing. Simple/Advanced toggle persists and is explicitly described as a display-depth change, not a different computation. Theme default is dark navy/forest with optional high contrast; unit changes convert only at display layer; time zone/locale are explicit. Reduced motion and map default layer are optional preferences.

## 74. Privacy and profile

Explain which data remains local, which remote providers receive a request, which small snapshot is uploaded for scheduled analysis, what public regional sharing includes and how to revoke it. Background scheduling and public sharing are off by default. If sign-in/sync is added, explicitly state which records are uploaded. When switching accounts, do not display the previous user's data for even one frame. No cross-device sync claim without an implemented sync API.

Separate dangerous operations: delete farm, delete all local data, revoke background processing, revoke public sharing and delete account. Each confirmation lists exact scope and remote-copy/backup retention. Export first where appropriate. Deletion is complete only after actual acknowledgment; pending state identifies what remains.

## 75. Global search

Search authorized farms, fields, crop names, rotation plans, reports, alerts, tasks and evidence. Results show type icon, exact title and farm/field context. Debounce queries, support keyboard arrows/enter/escape, retain recent local searches if privacy setting allows and preserve stable IDs when navigating. Empty result tells user categories searched and offers relevant create action. Never search another user's private farms.

## 76. Notifications drawer

Right-side drawer on desktop and full-height sheet on mobile. Header with title, unread count, mark-all-read and filters. Group by date/severity. Each item shows title, evidence-backed summary, farm/field, timestamp, read/unread, alert lifecycle and actions. `Mark read` differs from `Dismiss` and `Resolve`. Opening selects exact farm/field/alert. Repeated schedule runs referencing one continuing risk should update/deduplicate the same alert rather than create notification spam.

## 77. AI Agronomist

Shared side panel with context chip such as `Field 2 · Rotation Plan A`; user can change context. Send only the minimum validated context required to the backend, not the entire local store. The assistant can explain evidence and guide navigation but cannot mutate farm data, activate a plan, or commit parsed farmer practices without explicit confirmation. Quantitative claims link to report/evidence IDs. Distinguish stored facts, computed estimates and suggested interpretations. On provider failure preserve draft and show a usable fallback; no fake successful response. Sanitize output and treat user/external text as untrusted input.

## 78. Page guide

A `? Guide` action on main pages opens page-specific help: purpose, how to read key elements, metrics/score definitions, available actions, data limitations and deeper links. Use curated content connected to the actual screen rather than unsupported generative explanations. Provide focus trap, escape-to-close and focus return.

